    {
      "root_cause_candidate": "The vulnerability arises from using integer division to calculate `ENTRIES_PER_PAGE` (`PAGE_SIZE / ENTRY_SIZE`), which discards remainder bytes and causes incorrect assumptions about page group capacity during high-order memory allocations in the ftrace subsystem.",
      "evidence_points": "The patch removes the `ENTRIES_PER_PAGE` macro and replaces its usage in `ftrace_allocate_records()` and `ftrace_process_locs()` with byte-based calculations (`count * ENTRY_SIZE / PAGE_SIZE` and `(PAGE_SIZE << order) / ENTRY_SIZE`) to accurately reflect actual page capacity."
    },
